Short:        MegaBall 4, registered version
Author:       Ed Mackey and Al Mackey
Uploader:     Aminet Team <aminet aminet net>
Type:         game/misc
Architecture: m68k-amigaos

Ed and Al Mackey's famous Breakout version "MegaBall", as found on the
author's website:

http://www.almackey.com/#MegaBall

MegaBall is now licensed under the Apache 2.0 license, the sources are
available in a separate archive.

Original readme as found in the archive following below:


This is the official distibution of the MegaBall V4.0 ADF files from Ed and Al
Mackey. MegaBall works with only a few emulators (the most recent releases of
UAE do it nicely) due to some of its sound initialization routines -- ironicly
put there to make MegaBall compatible with future Amiga hardware.

Unlike most Amiga ADFs you'll find MegaBall cannot be ran directly from the
floppies. It's best that you make a directory on your hard drive somewhere
where you have some space, and make a virtual hard drive to use it (in WinUAE,
this is done on the "Hard Drives" panel, with the "Add Directory" button).
Once you install Workbench on the hard drive, reboot the emulator from it.
Then, insert the three floppies and use the installer on the first one to
install MegaBall to the hard drive. For MegaBall to work, the sound emulation
mode must be set to "Emulated, 100% accurate".

Watch for new releases from the Mackey Brothers at Blinkenlichten Productions!

Al Mackey
August 15, 2001
